# Text is LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf
# says. Several files are checked byte for byte: calendar data against its
# published checksum, research records parsed line by line by the reference
# tests, and the inference runtime against its SHA-256 fingerprint. A Windows
# checkout that turned them into CRLF broke all three.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Offline assets are served exactly as committed; their bytes are what the
# fingerprints in the tool registry describe, so they are never converted.
public/assets/offline/** -text

*.onnx binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
